            </classificationInformation>
            <common:generalComment xml:lang="en">For operation is meant the input of the waste and the refilling of the tunnels. The waste volume includes always the container. The density of ILW is approximately 2.5 tonne per m3. The total electricity supplied from the grid has been estimated from information on the power and the duration of operations given for the early design of a Swiss LAW repository, adjusted to the new waste inventory. For the transport of the radioactive waste, an average distance of 100 km has been considered. The burdens associated with this repository are allocated to the total amount of radioactive waste, mostly produced by nuclear power plants, but also by medicine and industry.;
Synonyms: Low and intermediate level long-lived radioactive waste; 
UUID: 0004e814-c18d-42e2-a3f7-ce1fa51a3c2c</common:generalComment>
